course: dictionary
lesson: 12692
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one fits. «The road was closed, so we followed a diversion through the village.» Here a diversion is a different route for traffic.
explain: «The magician made a loud bang as a diversion, so nobody noticed the rabbit disappearing.» The bang took everyone's attention away from what was really happening. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: «The water was sent along a new diversion into a field.» Here the word means turning something to another direction. «Reading a funny book was a welcome diversion after the test.» That means something fun that passes the time. Same word, different jobs.
fact: A diversion is a different route that traffic must take when the usual road is closed.
fact: A diversion can also be something that takes attention away from what is really happening, often on purpose.
fact: In a story, a character might create a diversion to distract the guards.
fact: A diversion can be the act of turning a river or money to another direction or use.
fact: A welcome diversion is something fun that passes the time. Americans say «detour» for a road diversion.
exercise: «The motorway was closed, so the driver followed the diversion.» What is a diversion here? | A kind of loud noise | *A different route for traffic | A river that has dried up | A fun game
exercise: «The thief created a diversion so the guards looked the other way.» What does diversion mean? | A way of turning water | A road that is closed | *Something that takes attention away | A fun party
exercise: «Reading a funny book was a welcome diversion after the test.» What does diversion mean? | Turning a river | *Something fun that passes time | A hidden trap | A different route
test: «The bridge was closed, so the bus took a diversion through the hills.» Which meaning fits? | A tall building | Something sad | *A different road to go round the closed bridge | A loud sound made on purpose
test: «The water was sent along a new diversion to the farm.» What does diversion mean here? | A game with cards | Something fun | *The act of turning water to another direction | A kind of hat
exam: «Her sudden cough was a clever diversion while the others slipped out.» What does diversion mean? | A fun song | A road sign | A river channel | *Something that takes attention away from what really happens
